5	1165,598,1681,1048	Fig. 5.	The corolla of the Morning-Glory, taken off whole: a wide funnel with a wavy, spreading rim and a narrow tube below, shown about natural size.
6	1340,1072,1512,1286	Fig. 6.	The calyx of the Morning-Glory alone: a small green cup of narrow pointed sepals on a short stalk.
7	958,1496,1676,2020	Fig. 7.	The Morning-Glory corolla split down and spread open, showing the five stamens growing from its base, each a slender filament tipped with an anther.
